      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "THE MATH  &  THE CONFIG RELATIONSHIPS",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "THE MATH  &  THE CONFIG RELATIONSHIPS",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el1118",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 1017.6,
      "y": 1557.85,
      "width": 562.8,
      "height": 490.0,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 8853442,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 117087022,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "  8,000 rps x 90 s        =  720,000 orders\n  WMS ceiling             =      200 orders/sec\n  DRAIN TIME              =    3,600 s  =  1 HOUR of backlog\n\n  Little's Law  (WMS p99 = 300 ms, batch = 10, sequential):\n     per invocation :  10 x 300 ms        =  3.0 s\n     throughput     :  10 / 3.0           =  3.33 orders/s/instance\n     for 200/s      :  200 / 3.33         =  60 concurrent\n     ESM setting    :  45   <- 25% headroom; never run at 100%\n\n  THE RELATIONSHIPS  (six independent numbers scores badly):\n\n     visibilityTimeout  >=  6 x lambdaTimeout\n     lambdaTimeout      >=  batchSize x wmsTimeout + overhead\n     retryBudget = maxReceive x VT  >=  expected WMS outage\n     maxConcurrency     <=  wmsRate / (batch / batchDuration)\n     ddbTtl > partnerRetryWindow + retryBudget + drainTime\n            > 24 h + 25 min + 1 h            ->  set 7 DAYS\n\n  IDEMPOTENCY -- three layers:\n     1. SQS MessageDeduplicationId ...... retry storms < 5 min\n     2. DynamoDB conditional write ...... everything beyond\n     3. orderId passed to WMS ........... your own crash retries\n\n  Write intent (WMS_SENT) BEFORE the side effect. Call-first\n  means you can ship an order with no record that you did.\n  Write-first turns \"did it happen?\" into \"call it again,\n  idempotently\" -- which is always safe.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "  8,000 rps x 90 s        =  720,000 orders\n  WMS ceiling             =      200 orders/sec\n  DRAIN TIME              =    3,600 s  =  1 HOUR of backlog\n\n  Little's Law  (WMS p99 = 300 ms, batch = 10, sequential):\n     per invocation :  10 x 300 ms        =  3.0 s\n     throughput     :  10 / 3.0           =  3.33 orders/s/instance\n     for 200/s      :  200 / 3.33         =  60 concurrent\n     ESM setting    :  45   <- 25% headroom; never run at 100%\n\n  THE RELATIONSHIPS  (six independent numbers scores badly):\n\n     visibilityTimeout  >=  6 x lambdaTimeout\n     lambdaTimeout      >=  batchSize x wmsTimeout + overhead\n     retryBudget = maxReceive x VT  >=  expected WMS outage\n     maxConcurrency     <=  wmsRate / (batch / batchDuration)\n     ddbTtl > partnerRetryWindow + retryBudget + drainTime\n            > 24 h + 25 min + 1 h            ->  set 7 DAYS\n\n  IDEMPOTENCY -- three layers:\n     1. SQS MessageDeduplicationId ...... retry storms < 5 min\n     2. DynamoDB conditional write ...... everything beyond\n     3. orderId passed to WMS ........... your own crash retries\n\n  Write intent (WMS_SENT) BEFORE the side effect. Call-first\n  means you can ship an order with no record that you did.\n  Write-first turns \"did it happen?\" into \"call it again,\n  idempotently\" -- which is always safe.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el1120",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 2034.0,
      "y": 1482.25,
      "width": 700,
      "height": 790,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#e03131",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
