      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 18,
      "fontFamily": 1,
      "text": "THREE DEFECTS THE NAIVE DESIGN SHIPS WITH",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "THREE DEFECTS THE NAIVE DESIGN SHIPS WITH",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el1124",
      "type": "text",
      "x": 2067.6,
      "y": 1557.85,
      "width": 495.59999999999997,
      "height": 612.5,
      "angle": 0,
      "strokeColor": "#343a40",
      "backgroundColor": "transparent",
      "fillStyle": "solid",
      "strokeWidth": 1,
      "strokeStyle": "solid",
      "roughness": 1,
      "opacity": 100,
      "groupIds": [],
      "frameId": null,
      "roundness": null,
      "seed": 8900956,
      "version": 1,
      "versionNonce": 117715396,
      "isDeleted": false,
      "boundElements": [],
      "updated": 1,
      "link": null,
      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "1   FIFO THROUGHPUT  --  fatal\n    Default FIFO = 300 TPS per API action\n    (3,000 msg/s only if you batch 10 per send).\n    One message per HTTP request = 300/s. You need 8,000.\n    26x over -> ThrottlingException -> 500 -> partner\n    retries -> load INCREASES. Failure is not graceful.\n    FIX: high-throughput FIFO, both attributes.\n    CAVEAT: throughput scales with the NUMBER of message\n    groups. One whale customer = one group = serialised\n    by definition. Composite key customerId#shardN, and\n    admit you weakened ordering to per-shard.\n\n2   DLQ -> FIFO REDRIVE  --  silent correctness bug\n    A1 fails 3x -> DLQ. A2, A3 were BLOCKED behind it.\n    Group unblocks, A2 and A3 process. Then you redrive A1.\n    A1 now executes AFTER A2 and A3. Ordering violated,\n    silently, by something that looks like best practice.\n\n3   NO BACKPRESSURE ON A 200 rps DOWNSTREAM\n    Nothing caps the consumer. The ESM scales out and\n    hammers a dying API -> 5xx -> maxReceiveCount ->\n    VALID orders land in the DLQ because WMS was busy.\n    You lose orders to someone else's outage.\n\nAND THE TWO CLAIMS THAT SOUND RIGHT:\n\n  \"FIFO gives exactly-once processing\"\n     No -- exactly-once DELIVERY, 5 min window. The queue\n     cannot know your side effects ran. Crash after the\n     WMS call, before delete -> you call WMS twice.\n\n  \"The DLQ solves the poison pill\"\n     It bounds it, at 5 x 300 s = 25 MINUTES of frozen\n     orders for that customer. It is the last line of\n     defence, not the fix. Classify the failure instead.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "1   FIFO THROUGHPUT  --  fatal\n    Default FIFO = 300 TPS per API action\n    (3,000 msg/s only if you batch 10 per send).\n    One message per HTTP request = 300/s. You need 8,000.\n    26x over -> ThrottlingException -> 500 -> partner\n    retries -> load INCREASES. Failure is not graceful.\n    FIX: high-throughput FIFO, both attributes.\n    CAVEAT: throughput scales with the NUMBER of message\n    groups. One whale customer = one group = serialised\n    by definition. Composite key customerId#shardN, and\n    admit you weakened ordering to per-shard.\n\n2   DLQ -> FIFO REDRIVE  --  silent correctness bug\n    A1 fails 3x -> DLQ. A2, A3 were BLOCKED behind it.\n    Group unblocks, A2 and A3 process. Then you redrive A1.\n    A1 now executes AFTER A2 and A3. Ordering violated,\n    silently, by something that looks like best practice.\n\n3   NO BACKPRESSURE ON A 200 rps DOWNSTREAM\n    Nothing caps the consumer. The ESM scales out and\n    hammers a dying API -> 5xx -> maxReceiveCount ->\n    VALID orders land in the DLQ because WMS was busy.\n    You lose orders to someone else's outage.\n\nAND THE TWO CLAIMS THAT SOUND RIGHT:\n\n  \"FIFO gives exactly-once processing\"\n     No -- exactly-once DELIVERY, 5 min window. The queue\n     cannot know your side effects ran. Crash after the\n     WMS call, before delete -> you call WMS twice.\n\n  \"The DLQ solves the poison pill\"\n     It bounds it, at 5 x 300 s = 25 MINUTES of frozen\n     orders for that customer. It is the last line of\n     defence, not the fix. Classify the failure instead.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    },
    {
      "id": "el1126",
      "type": "rectangle",
      "x": 60.0,
      "y": 1482.25,
