      "locked": false,
      "fontSize": 14,
      "fontFamily": 3,
      "text": "*  202 Accepted, never 200 OK. Backlog is one hour;\n   200 implies fulfilment you cannot honour.\n*  Idempotency-Key header is MANDATORY -> 400 if absent.\n   The PARTNER supplies it. If you mint a UUID server-side,\n   a retry produces a new id and dedup is decorative.\n*  Same key + different payloadHash -> 422 + alarm\n   (that is a partner bug, not a duplicate).\n*  GET /orders/{orderId} for terminal status, plus\n   EventBridge / webhook on completion + rejection.\n*  Payloads > 256 KB -> presigned S3, send the key.\n\nTHE HONEST CONCLUSION\n\nIf the business needs sub-minute fulfilment at 8,000 rps,\nthe architecture is not the constraint -- THE WMS IS.\nNo AWS design removes a 200 rps vendor ceiling. That is a\nconversation about a bulk endpoint or a higher rate limit.",
      "textAlign": "left",
      "verticalAlign": "top",
      "containerId": null,
      "originalText": "*  202 Accepted, never 200 OK. Backlog is one hour;\n   200 implies fulfilment you cannot honour.\n*  Idempotency-Key header is MANDATORY -> 400 if absent.\n   The PARTNER supplies it. If you mint a UUID server-side,\n   a retry produces a new id and dedup is decorative.\n*  Same key + different payloadHash -> 422 + alarm\n   (that is a partner bug, not a duplicate).\n*  GET /orders/{orderId} for terminal status, plus\n   EventBridge / webhook on completion + rejection.\n*  Payloads > 256 KB -> presigned S3, send the key.\n\nTHE HONEST CONCLUSION\n\nIf the business needs sub-minute fulfilment at 8,000 rps,\nthe architecture is not the constraint -- THE WMS IS.\nNo AWS design removes a 200 rps vendor ceiling. That is a\nconversation about a bulk endpoint or a higher rate limit.",
      "lineHeight": 1.25,
      "autoResize": true
    }
  ],
